{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'pwd; ls -la; find .. -name AGENTS.md -print; cat VENUE.md; cat /workspace/paper/.codex/skills/{write-paper-standalone,validate-paper,memory-log,scientific-evidence,generate-concept-figure}/SKILL.md'","aggregated_output":"/workspace/paper\ntotal 1084\ndrwx------ 6 agent agent   4096 Nov  7 06:38 .\ndrwx------ 9 agent agent   4096 Nov  7 06:26 ..\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    747 Nov  7 06:26 .agentic_paper_workspace.json\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent   4096 Nov  7 06:26 .codex\nprw------- 1 agent agent      0 Nov  7 06:38 .paper_stream_20261107_062605.fifo\n-rw------- 1 agent agent      0 Nov  7 06:26 .paper_two_stage_enabled\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   3685 Nov  7 06:38 VENUE.md\ndrwx------ 2 agent agent   4096 Nov  7 06:26 figures\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 agent agent     16 Nov  7 06:26 global_memory -> ../investigation\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  12191 Nov  7 06:26 global_memory_recent.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   4950 Nov  7 06:26 global_memory_summary.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   6443 Nov  7 06:37 memory.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent  26973 Nov  2 14:28 paper.bst\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   8934 Nov  2 14:28 paper.sty\n-rw------- 1 agent agent      0 Nov  7 06:38 paper_agent_codex_20261107_062605.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  39817 Nov  7 06:26 paper_data.json\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent   4096 Nov  7 06:29 paper_diagnostics\n-rw------- 1 agent agent      0 Nov  7 06:26 paper_diagnostics_20261107_062605_46655.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   4332 Nov  7 06:38 paper_events_20261107_062605.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    791 Nov  7 06:26 paper_prep_20261107_062605.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  69534 Nov  7 06:38 paper_prompt.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent  26021 Nov  7 06:37 paper_strategy.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent  22257 Nov  7 06:37 paper_strategy.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 436984 Nov  7 06:37 paper_strategy_agent_codex_20261107_062605.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  44467 Nov  7 06:30 paper_strategy_prompt.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    331 Nov  7 06:37 paper_strategy_resolution.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   7365 Nov  7 06:29 reference_query_plan.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   9290 Nov  7 06:29 reference_query_plan.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 227013 Nov  7 06:29 reference_query_plan_agent_codex_20261107_062605.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  29673 Nov  7 06:26 reference_query_plan_prompt.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    265 Nov  7 06:29 reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    279 Nov  7 06:29 reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   2918 Nov  7 06:30 reference_retrieval.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   9130 Nov  7 06:30 references.bib\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  28451 Nov  7 06:30 references_provenance.json\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 agent agent     16 Nov  7 06:26 results -> ../investigation\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent   4096 Nov  7 06:26 source_evidence\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    265 Nov  7 06:37 strategy_validation_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    271 Nov  7 06:37 strategy_validation_feedback.md\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 agent agent      7 Nov  7 06:26 task -> ../task\n../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/vercel/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/supabase-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/data-analytics/AGENTS.md\n../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/zoom/AGENTS.md\n../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/prototype/AGENTS.md\n../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/mobile-app/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/vercel/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/supabase-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/data-analytics/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/zoom/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/prototype/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/mobile-app/AGENTS.md\n# ICLR 2026 Venue Brief\n\nUse this brief to tailor the manuscript for the International Conference on Learning\nRepresentations 2026 submission.\n\n## Hard Constraints\n- Target venue: ICLR 2026.\n- Submission type: conference paper.\n- Body-page budget: 8 to 9 pages, excluding references. A body of 8 pages counts only when its final page is at least 75% full; a shorter or sparser body fails validation.\n- Review model: double-blind. The submission must be fully anonymized.\n- Omit author names, affiliations, acknowledgements, and funding statements from the manuscript.\n- Do not include self-identifying links such as personal repositories, lab pages, or internal URLs.\n- Refer to your own prior work in the third person; never write phrasing that reveals authorship.\n- Include a separate `LLM Usage` section, which may appear in the appendix, describing the precise role\n  of LLMs in research ideation and writing. Significant LLM use must be disclosed; nondisclosure can\n  cause desk rejection.\n- The paper must satisfy the ICLR template and formatting rules selected by `--paper-format iclr`.\n\n## Audience\n- Machine learning researchers working on representation learning, optimization, architectures, and\n  empirical methodology.\n- Readers expect a clearly stated contribution, honest baselines, controlled comparisons, ablations\n  that isolate the mechanism, and explicit statements of scope and limitations.\n- Reviewers reward reproducibility and calibrated claims far more than headline numbers.\n\n## Framing Priorities\n- Lead with the research question and the specific claim the evidence supports.\n- State the contribution precisely in the abstract and introduction: what is new, what it improves,\n  and under which conditions.\n- Motivate the method mechanistically. Explain why it should work, not only that it does.\n- Support the central claim with controlled comparisons against meaningful baselines.\n- Use ablations to attribute the gain to the proposed component rather than to incidental changes.\n- Report variance across seeds or runs whenever the artifacts provide it.\n- Be explicit about the regime studied and where the result is not expected to hold.\n\n## Manuscript Guidance\n- Prefer a title and abstract that name the mechanism and the setting, not a generic improvement claim.\n- In the introduction, make the contribution list concrete and verifiable against the artifacts.\n- In the method section, give enough detail to reimplement: objective, architecture, and the\n  hyperparameters that matter.\n- In the results section, foreground controlled comparisons, ablations, sensitivity, and failure modes.\n- Include a limitations discussion that a reviewer would otherwise raise.\n- Figures must meet top-tier conference standards in both design (clean typography, consistent colors,\n  proper labels and legends, high resolution) and scientific content (clear message, no filler).\n- The template is single-column: size figures for the full text width and keep axis labels legible.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n- Do not deanonymize the submission in any way.\n- Do not overclaim generality beyond the settings actually evaluated.\n- Do not present a benchmark delta as a mechanistic insight without evidence connecting the two.\n- Do not omit baselines or ablations that the grounded artifacts already support.\n- Do not describe results as state of the art unless the comparison in the artifacts establishes it.\n- Do not pad the paper to fill the page budget.\n\n## Decision Rule\n- When venue framing and grounded evidence conflict, follow the grounded evidence.\n- Use this brief to choose emphasis, terminology, and narrative framing, not to invent stronger claims\n  than the run supports.\ncat: /workspace/paper/.codex/skills/{write-paper-standalone,validate-paper,memory-log,scientific-evidence,generate-concept-figure}/SKILL.md: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
