ion{Introduction}\nReplace with grounded motivation, problem framing, and contributions.\n\n\\section{Related Work}\nSummarize relevant prior work using citation keys present in references.bib (for example, \\citep{templateReference2026}).\n\n\\section{Method}\nDescribe data, setup, and method details needed for reproducibility.\n\n\\section{Results}\nReport grounded quantitative and qualitative findings. Include figures and tables when useful.\n\n\\section{Conclusion}\nState key findings, limitations, and next steps supported by evidence.\n\n% IMPORTANT: \\clearpage flushes all pending floats before references so that\n% body-page counting excludes reference-only pages.  Do NOT remove.\n\\clearpage\n\\bibliography{references}\n\\bibliographystyle{paper}\n\n\\clearpage\n\\appendix\n\\section{Supplementary Information}\n% REQUIRED: Replace this scaffold with substantive grounded content.\n\\subsection{Reproducibility Details}\nReplace with grounded extended methods, reproducibility details, additional analyses, or supporting tables and figures.\n\n\\end{document}\n     1\t\"\"\"Deterministic CPU masked-factor starter; single-file finite-JSON handle API.\n     2\t\n     3\tAll requests and responses are objects. No additional response keys are allowed.\n     4\tEvery independent episode begins with reset; reset erases uploads, fits, contexts,\n     5\tand RNG. Seeds are arbitrary nonnegative integers, never workload selectors.\n     6\t\n     7\treset: {op:'reset', seed:int} -> {ok:true}.\n     8\ttrain_start: {op:'train_start', rows:int<=8192, columns:int<=1024,\n     9\t column_names:list[str] of length columns, training_steps:int in [1,100],\n    10\t max_queries:int<=8} -> {ok:true}. Allocates candidate-owned RAM only.\n    11\ttrain_chunk: {op:'train_chunk', offset:int, shape:[r,columns], dtype:'<f8',\n    12\t encoding:'base64', data:str, mask_dtype:'|u1', mask:str} -> {ok:true}.\n    13\tChunks are sequential, r<=256, at most 32 chunks. data contains row-major\n    14\tlittle-endian float64 normalized scores in [0,1]; mask is row-major uint8 0/1.\n    15\tUnobserved cells contain zero, not NaN. Decode both; masked cells are unknown.\n    16\ttrain_commit: {op:'train_commit'} -> {ok:true}; requires all rows uploaded.\n    17\tfit: {op:'fit'} -> {ok:true}; learn only from the committed historical matrix.\n    18\tstart: {op:'start', availability:list[list[bool]], max_queries:int} -> {ok:true}.\n    19\tCreates/replaces a batch of 1..128 independent new-model contexts; each mask has\n    20\tcolumns entries. A true entry may be purchased once; no scores are provided.\n    21\tselect: {op:'select'} -> {indices:list[int]}, exactly one unqueried available\n    22\tcolumn per active row. Rows have enough available columns for max_queries+1.\n    23\tobserve: {op:'observe', indices:list[int], values:list[float]} -> {ok:true}.\n    24\tExactly the last selections and their purchased normalized scores are supplied.\n    25\tOnly completed observations can affect subsequent decisions. Never pool contexts.\n    26\tpredict: {op:'predict'} -> {predictions:list[list[float]]}, shape [batch,columns],\n    27\tall entries finite numeric (not bool); evaluator clips to [0,1] and scores only\n    28\tavailable unpurchased entries. No diagnostics, state flags, or artifact paths.\n    29\t\n    30\tCalls follow reset, train_start, chunks, train_commit, fit, then repeated start /\n    31\t(select,observe,[predict])* trajectories. Prediction checkpoints and workload are\n    32\toperation-driven, not seed-driven. Fit allowance is advisory sweeps, not telemetry.\n    33\tThe starter fits a regularized masked latent model, selects rank using held-out\n    34\thistorical cells, and uses covariance-trace information selection with conditional\n    35\tridge reconstruction. It is a reproducible starting point, not a claimed win.\n    36\tNo filesystem or network transport is part of this interface. Full messages,\n    37\tincluding JSON framing, must be strictly below 64 MiB. Dependencies are preinstalled.\n    38\t\"\"\"\n    39\timport base64\n    40\timport numpy as np\n    41\t\n    42\t_STATE = {}\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\tdef factor_fit(values, mask, rank, steps, seed):\n    46\t    mean = np.sum(values * mask, axis=0) / np.maximum(mask.sum(axis=0), 1)\n    47\t    centered = values - mean\n    48\t    filled = np.where(mask, centered, 0.0)\n    49\t    _, singular, right = np.linalg.svd(filled, full_matrices=False)\n    50\t    factors = right[:rank].T * np.sqrt(np.maximum(singular[:rank], 1e-8))\n    51\t    latent = np.zeros((len(values), rank))\n    52\t    regularizer = np.eye(rank) * 0.1\n    53\t    for sweep in range(steps):\n    54\t        for row in range(len(values)):\n    55\t            selected = factors[mask[row]]\n    56\t            latent[row] = np.linalg.solve(selected.T @ selected + regularizer,\n    57\t                                          selected.T @ centered[row, mask[row]])\n    58\t        for column in range(values.shape[1]):\n    59\t            selected = latent[mask[:, column]]\n    60\t            factors[column] = np.linalg.solve(selected.T @ selected + regularizer,\n    61\t                                              selected.T @ centered[mask[:, column], column])\n    62\t    return mean, factors\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\tdef learn(values, mask, steps, seed):\n    66\t    random = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    67\t    validation = (random.random(mask.shape) < 0.1) & mask\n    68\t    fitting = mask & ~validation\n    69\t    best = None\n    70\t    for rank in (1, 2, 4, 8):\n    71\t        if rank > min(values.shape) - 1:\n    72\t            continue\n    73\t        mean, factors = factor_fit(values, fitting, rank, min(steps, 4), seed)\n    74\t        losses = []\n    75\t        for row in range(len(values)):\n    76\t            selected = factors[fitting[row]]\n    77\t            latent = np.linalg.solve(selected.T @ selected + np.eye(rank) * 0.1,\n    78\t                                     selected.T @ (values[row, fitting[row]] - mean[fitting[row]]))\n    79\t            losses.extend(np.abs((mean + factors @ latent - values[row])[validation[row]]))\n    80\t        loss = float(np.mean(losses)) if losses else 1.0\n    81\t        if best is None or loss < best[0]:\n    82\t            best = (loss, rank)\n    83\t    return factor_fit(values, mask, best[1], min(steps, 8), seed)\n    84\t\n    85\t\n    86\tdef handle(request):\n    87\t    operation = request['op']\n    88\t    if operation == 'reset':\n    89\t        _STATE.clear()\n    90\t        _STATE['seed'] = request['seed']\n    91\t        return {'ok': True}\n    92\t    if operation == 'train_start':\n    93\t        _STATE.update(values=np.zeros((request['rows'], request['columns'])),\n    94\t                      mask=np.zeros((request['rows'], request['columns']), dtype=bool),\n    95\t                      offset=0, steps=request['training_steps'])\n    96\t    elif operation == 'train_chunk':\n    97\t        shape = tuple(request['shape'])\n    98\t        values = np.frombuffer(base64.b64decode(request['data']), dtype='<f8').reshape(shape)\n    99\t        mask = np.frombuffer(base64.b64decode(request['mask']), dtype='u1').reshape(shape).astype(bool)\n   100\t        offset = request['offset']\n   101\t        _STATE['values'][offset:offset + shape[0]] = values\n   102\t        _STATE['mask'][offset:offset + shape[0]] = mask\n   103\t        _STATE['offset'] += shape[0]\n   104\t    elif operation == 'train_commit':\n   105\t        if _STATE['offset'] != len(_STATE['values']):\n   106\t            raise ValueError('incomplete training upload')\n   107\t    elif operation == 'fit':\n   108\t        mean, factors = learn(_STATE['values'], _STATE['mask'], _STATE['steps'], _STATE['seed'])\n   109\t        _STATE.update(mean=mean, factors=factors)\n   110\t    elif operation == 'start':\n   111\t        _STATE['available'] = np.array(request['availability'], dtype=bool)\n   112\t        _STATE['queried'] = np.zeros_like(_STATE['available'])\n   113\t        _STATE['observed'] = np.zeros(_STATE['available'].shape)\n   114\t    elif operation == 'select':\n   115\t        factors = _STATE['factors']\n   116\t        indices = []\n   117\t        for row in range(len(_STATE['available'])):\n   118\t            selected = factors[_STATE['queried'][row]]\n   119\t            covariance = np.linalg.inv(selected.T @ selected + np.eye(factors.shape[1]) * 0.1)\n   120\t            targets = factors[_STATE['available'][row] & ~_STATE['queried'][row]]\n   121\t            reduction = np.sum((targets @ covariance @ factors.T) ** 2, axis=0)\n   122\t            reduction /= 1.0 + np.sum((factors @ covariance) * factors, axis=1)\n   123\t            legal = _STATE['available'][row] & ~_STATE['queried'][row]\n   124\t            reduction[~legal] = -np.inf\n   125\t            indices.append(int(np.argmax(reduction)))\n   126\t        _STATE['pending'] = indices\n   127\t        return {'indices': indices}\n   128\t    elif operation == 'observe':\n   129\t        if request['indices'] != _STATE['pending']:\n   130\t            raise ValueError('unexpected observation')\n   131\t        for row, (column, value) in enumerate(zip(request['indices'], request['values'])):\n   132\t            _STATE['queried'][row, column] = True\n   133\t            _STATE['observed'][row, column] = value\n   134\t    elif operation == 'predict':\n   135\t        mean, factors = _STATE['mean'], _STATE['factors']\n   136\t        predictions = []\n   137\t        for row in range(len(_STATE['available'])):\n   138\t            selected = factors[_STATE['queried'][row]]\n   139\t            latent = np.linalg.solve(selected.T @ selected + np.eye(factors.shape[1]) * 0.1,\n   140\t                                     selected.T @ (_STATE['observed'][row, _STATE['queried'][row]]\n   141\t                                                   - mean[_STATE['queried'][row]]))\n   142\t            predictions.append(np.clip(mean + factors @ latent, 0, 1).tolist())\n   143\t        return {'predictions': predictions}\n   144\t    else:\n   145\t        raise ValueError('unknown operation')\n   146\t    return {'ok': True}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
