{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat .codex/skills/retrieve-references/SKILL.md; bash .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh emit-bundle --root-dir .; sed -n '35,64p' source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py; python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('paper_data.json'));print('\\\\n'.join(p['grounding_sources']))\nr=json.load(open('references_provenance.json'));print('REFSHAPE',r.keys());print(json.dumps(r['references'][0],indent=2))\na=json.load(open('task/resources/final/audit.json'));print('AUDIT KEYS',a.keys()); print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in a.items() if k not in ['sources','models']},indent=2)[:4500])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat .codex/skills/retrieve-references/SKILL.md; bash .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh emit-bundle --root-dir .; sed -n '35,64p' source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py; python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('paper_data.json'));print('\\\\n'.join(p['grounding_sources']))\nr=json.load(open('references_provenance.json'));print('REFSHAPE',r.keys());print(json.dumps(r['references'][0],indent=2))\na=json.load(open('task/resources/final/audit.json'));print('AUDIT KEYS',a.keys()); print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in a.items() if k not in ['sources','models']},indent=2)[:4500])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: retrieve-references\ndescription: Retrieve grounded BibTeX references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (`scholarly`) and write references.bib plus provenance JSON for paper generation.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nFetch references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (via `scholarly`) and keep only real BibTeX entries.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- Final report/paper generation.\n- Related-work section needs grounded citations.\n\n# What to do\n1. Build focused search queries from task goal, method names, and top experiment ideas.\n2. Preferred path (Semantic Scholar Graph API):\n```bash\npython scripts/s2_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n3. Fallback path (OpenAlex):\n```bash\npython scripts/openalex_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --search-limit 10 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n   Optional:\n   - `--mailto you@example.com` to enter the OpenAlex polite pool\n   - Env fallback: `OPENALEX_EMAIL`\n4. Alternate path (Google Scholar API wrapper with `scholarly`):\n```bash\npython -m pip install scholarly\npython scripts/scholarly_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --search-limit 25 \\\n  --sort-by relevance \\\n  --proxy-mode auto \\\n  --delay-seconds 0.5 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n   Proxy options:\n   - `--proxy-mode auto|none|free|single`\n   - `--proxy-http <url>` / `--proxy-https <url>` for `single`\n   - Env fallbacks: `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_MODE`, `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_HTTP`, `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_HTTPS`\n   - Global `HTTP_PROXY` / `HTTPS_PROXY` are intentionally ignored to avoid accidental ambient proxying\n5. Require `S2_API_KEY` when available for `s2_fetch.py` (script reads env automatically).\n6. Keep only references with valid BibTeX and citation key.\n7. Dedupe by citation key and paper id.\n8. Fail hard if references found `< min-refs`.\n9. Use `s2_fetch.py` first for stability, `openalex_fetch.py` as the next fallback, and `scholarly_fetch.py` last if the other sources fail.\n\n# Outputs\n- `references.bib`\n- `references_provenance.json`\n\n# Notes\n- Use `templates/provenance.schema.json` for expected shape.\nWrote spec bundle to /workspace/paper/scientific-evidence\n- spec.md\n- schemas/evidence-reference.schema.json\n- schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json\n- schemas/ledger-entry.schema.json\n- schemas/verification-report.schema.json\n- bundle.manifest.json\n- ledger.jsonl\nridge reconstruction. It is a reproducible starting point, not a claimed win.\nNo filesystem or network transport is part of this interface. Full messages,\nincluding JSON framing, must be strictly below 64 MiB. Dependencies are preinstalled.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport numpy as np\n\n_STATE = {}\n\n\ndef factor_fit(values, mask, rank, steps, seed):\n    mean = np.sum(values * mask, axis=0) / np.maximum(mask.sum(axis=0), 1)\n    centered = values - mean\n    filled = np.where(mask, centered, 0.0)\n    _, singular, right = np.linalg.svd(filled, full_matrices=False)\n    factors = right[:rank].T * np.sqrt(np.maximum(singular[:rank], 1e-8))\n    latent = np.zeros((len(values), rank))\n    regularizer = np.eye(rank) * 0.1\n    for sweep in range(steps):\n        for row in range(len(values)):\n            selected = factors[mask[row]]\n            latent[row] = np.linalg.solve(selected.T @ selected + regularizer,\n                                          selected.T @ centered[row, mask[row]])\n        for column in range(values.shape[1]):\n            selected = latent[mask[:, column]]\n            factors[column] = np.linalg.solve(selected.T @ selected + regularizer,\n                                              selected.T @ centered[mask[:, column], column])\n    return mean, factors\n\n\nfinal.evidence.episodes\nfinal.metric.combined_score\nfinal.metric.constant_score\nfinal.metric.control_failure_fraction\nfinal.metric.copy_score\nfinal.metric.correct\nfinal.metric.corruption_gap\nfinal.metric.failed_episode_fraction\nfinal.metric.medoid_ridge_score\nfinal.metric.mteb_score\nfinal.metric.open_llm_score\nfinal.metric.paired_gain_ci_high\nfinal.metric.paired_gain_ci_low\nfinal.metric.permuted_score\nfinal.metric.random_lowrank_score\nfinal.metric.reset_replay_ok\nfinal.metric.selected_ridge_score\nfinal.qualification.correct\nfinal.qualification.outcome\nfinal.qualification.status\nresult.total_attempts\nresult.total_correct_programs\nresult.total_evaluated_programs\nresult.total_ideas\nstudy.attempts.scored\nstudy.attempts.total\nstudy.attempts.unscored\nstudy.baseline_score\nstudy.final.correct\nstudy.final.outcome\nstudy.final.status\nstudy.investigation_outcome\nstudy.search_score\nstudy.search_score_delta\nstudy.selection_kind\nREFSHAPE dict_keys(['campaign_results_dir', 'count', 'generated_at', 'queries', 'reference_query_plan', 'references', 'results_dir'])\n{\n  \"citation_count\": 330,\n  \"citation_key\": \"Zheng2013CollaborativeMF\",\n  \"id\": \"ref.s2.92e8f21bcf8437b6e6b7e43d4c2e9bd717e41673\",\n  \"paper_id\": \"92e8f21bcf8437b6e6b7e43d4c2e9bd717e41673\",\n  \"query\": \"\\\"matrix factorization\\\" \\\"alternating least squares\\\" \\\"collaborative filtering\\\" -\\\"language model\\\" -benchmark\",\n  \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-11-07T06:29:40.149431+00:00\",\n  \"source_url\": \"https://api.semanticscholar.org/graph/v1/paper/92e8f21bcf8437b6e6b7e43d4c2e9bd717e41673?fields=paperId%2Ctitle%2Cyear%2Cvenue%2CcitationCount%2CcitationStyles%2Curl\",\n  \"title\": \"Collaborative matrix factorization with multiple similarities for predicting drug-target interactions\",\n  \"venue\": \"Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining\",\n  \"year\": 2013\n}\nAUDIT KEYS dict_keys(['schema_version', 'normalization', 'split_rule', 'duplicate_raw_documents_omitted_before_split', 'cross_plane_intersections', 'own_counts', 'peer_commitments', 'sources', 'extraction'])\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"normalization\": \"NFKC, LF, whitespace-collapse before split; canonical finite JSON; identifiers omitted from complete score-example hashes\",\n  \"split_rule\": \"Connected family/alias/complete-score-example/raw-document groups; SHA256(plane-v1/min(source/id)) parity\",\n  \"duplicate_raw_documents_omitted_before_split\": 43,\n  \"cross_plane_intersections\": {\n    \"examples\": 0,\n    \"documents\": 0,\n    \"ids\": 0,\n    \"families\": 0\n  },\n  \"own_counts\": {\n    \"examples\": 2846,\n    \"documents\": 23743,\n    \"ids\": 2838,\n    \"families\": 732\n  },\n  \"peer_commitments\": {\n    \"examples\": \"14a96bcc6f13186c1a3358ad31afb58d2795965a541803df8e912bed477b3658\",\n    \"documents\": \"0dde36eb02ba7ebef2e38de3fd913b6b32ff70e91c5663564f5848bcc6acb318\",\n    \"ids\": \"741d372cc793d633a6c2759307e3f813972d77dd47a9e3a3c7f3a811afc77633\",\n    \"families\": \"466c5c009b9a621b2f60f1a906a4c733ad52fef7790a28fc79de4b47db3464c1\"\n  },\n  \"extraction\": \"MTEB original test main_score in natural [0,1], default/English subsets only, distinct task/dataset_revision/subset columns; deterministic lexicographic first revision on repeated model-column; omit nonfinite/out-of-bound scores, no score-based filtering beyond declared natural bounds. OLL six Raw columns, no aggregates. Raw file hashes retained; model example hashes use complete extracted scores before preprocessing. Exact duplicate raw MTEB documents retain lexicographic archive-first owner only; other copies excluded as missing before splitting. Family is namespace plus lowercase model stem before first punctuation/digit, from OLL Base Model when present. OLL complete table read: 4576 source rows. Full eligible production rows used.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
