{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"ls task; find task -maxdepth 3 -type f | head -40; cat scientific-evidence/spec.md | head -115; cat .codex/skills/retrieve-references/templates/provenance.schema.json | head -90; sed -n '1,100p' .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh; python - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('paper_strategy.json')); print(s['recommended_title']); print(s['central_thesis']); print(json.dumps(s['method_groups'],indent=2)); print(json.dumps(json.load(open('task/resources/final/audit.json'))['sources'],indent=2)[:2000]); print(json.dumps(json.load(open('task/resources/final/plan.json'))['production'],indent=2)[:1800])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"ls task; find task -maxdepth 3 -type f | head -40; cat scientific-evidence/spec.md | head -115; cat .codex/skills/retrieve-references/templates/provenance.schema.json | head -90; sed -n '1,100p' .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh; python - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('paper_strategy.json')); print(s['recommended_title']); print(s['central_thesis']); print(json.dumps(s['method_groups'],indent=2)); print(json.dumps(json.load(open('task/resources/final/audit.json'))['sources'],indent=2)[:2000]); print(json.dumps(json.load(open('task/resources/final/plan.json'))['production'],indent=2)[:1800])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"capture.py\nevaluate.py\nevaluate_final.py\nprogram_0\nrequirements.txt\nresources\ntask.md\ntask_contract.json\n# scientific-evidence\n\nThis is the canonical generated spec bundle for the `scientific-evidence` skill.\nUse the skill script as the source of truth for schemas, layout, and wording.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis contract is generic and file-format-agnostic.\nIt supports inline evidence refs in text-like files, adjacent `.prov.json` sidecars for generated artifacts, and a central JSONL ledger.\n\n## Why this exists\n\nThe point of `scientific-evidence` is to make an agent leave a machine-checkable trail for important numbers, figures, tables, and derived outputs.\nA paper or report should not depend on free-form prose alone when those claims can point back to real artifacts.\nAlways use this contract during paper writing whenever the agent adds manuscript numbers, table values, figure inputs, or derived statistics.\n\n## Fixed directory structure\n\n```text\nscientific-evidence/\n  spec.md\n  bundle.manifest.json\n  ledger.jsonl\n  schemas/\n    evidence-reference.schema.json\n    artifact-manifest.schema.json\n    ledger-entry.schema.json\n    verification-report.schema.json\n```\n\nAgents should use this layout exactly. Do not invent alternate bundle directories.\n\n## Grammar\n\n```text\nEvidenceRef   := '@evidence[[' Target [ '#' Locator ] ']]'\nTarget        := non-empty path | absolute path | URI | stable identifier\nLocator       := opaque fragment without closing ']]'\nSidecar       := '<artifact>.prov.json'\nLedger        := 'scientific-evidence/ledger.jsonl'\n```\n\n### Notes\n\n- `Target` stays generic. The verifier may classify it as `path`, `absolute-path`, `uri`, `id`, or `unknown`.\n- `Locator` is opaque unless a verifier adapter knows how to interpret it.\n- Text-like artifacts should use inline `@evidence[[...]]` refs. Binary or generated outputs should carry an adjacent `.prov.json` sidecar.\n\n### Minimal examples\n\n- `@evidence[[TARGET]]`\n- `@evidence[[TARGET#LOCATOR]]`\n- `figure.png.prov.json`\n\n## Verification behavior\n\nA verifier uses this bundle to inspect whether the agent left a connected evidence trail.\nThe base verifier uses three reference states:\n\n- `resolved`: the target exists and the verifier can validate the locator semantics it understands.\n- `anchored`: the target exists, but only path/hash checks were possible or the locator remained opaque.\n- `dangling`: the target does not resolve, the sidecar chain breaks, or the reference is malformed.\n\n### Minimum verifier expectations\n\n1. Resolve every inline evidence ref to a target path, URI, or id when possible.\n2. Mark each ref as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`.\n3. For manifests, require every `derived_from` edge to resolve to at least `anchored`.\n4. When hashes are recorded, compare them. Missing hashes are allowed.\n5. Do not pretend to interpret unknown locator grammars. Keep them `anchored` unless an adapter proves more.\n\n### What verification should prove\n\nAt a minimum, a downstream verifier should be able to:\n\n- scan text-like artifacts for `@evidence[[...]]` refs\n- read `.prov.json` sidecars for generated artifacts\n- resolve refs against real files or stable ids\n- classify each link as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`\n- fail when a generated artifact has no input trail or when a claimed source does not exist\n\nThis does not prove every scientific claim automatically. It proves whether the agent left enough structure for later auditing and stricter replay.\nA core paper-writing policy is: do not hardcode result numbers inside plotting or calculation scripts when those values should come from real artifacts. Read from files and leave matching `@evidence[[...]]` refs near the read or derivation logic.\n\n## Schema set\n\nThe generated bundle includes:\n\n- `schemas/evidence-reference.schema.json`\n- `schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json`\n- `schemas/ledger-entry.schema.json`\n- `schemas/verification-report.schema.json`\n- `spec.md`\n- `bundle.manifest.json`\n- `ledger.jsonl`\n\n### Schema intent\n\n- `evidence-reference`: parsed form of one inline `@evidence[[...]]` token.\n- `artifact-manifest`: canonical sidecar schema for `<artifact>.prov.json`.\n- `ledger-entry`: one JSONL row in `scientific-evidence/ledger.jsonl`.\n- `verification-report`: verifier output with per-reference results and summary counts.\n\n## Examples across file formats\n\n### Python\n\n```python\n# Read the metric from disk; do not hardcode 96.7 here.\n# @evidence[[results/metrics.json#mnist.accuracy_mean]]\nimport json\npayload = json.loads(open(\"results/metrics.json\", encoding=\"utf-8\").read())\nvalue = payload[\"mnist\"][\"accuracy_mean\"]\n```\n\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"ReferenceProvenance\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"generated_at\", \"count\", \"queries\", \"references\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"generated_at\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n    \"count\": {\"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 0},\n    \"queries\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n    },\n    \"references\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"id\", \"paper_id\", \"citation_key\", \"query\", \"source_url\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"id\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n          \"paper_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n          \"citation_key\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n          \"title\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n          \"year\": {\"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"]},\n          \"venue\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n          \"citation_count\": {\"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"]},\n          \"query\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n          \"source_url\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n          \"retrieved_at\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n#!/bin/bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nif [ $# -ne 1 ]; then\n  echo \"Usage: bash compile_latex.sh <paper.tex>\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nTEX_ARGUMENT=\"$1\"\nif [ ! -f \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\" ]; then\n  echo \"Missing TeX file: $TEX_ARGUMENT\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nif ! command -v pdflatex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdflatex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v bibtex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: bibtex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: python3\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v pdftotext >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdftotext\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nPAPER_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\" && pwd)\"\nTEX_FILE=\"$(basename \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\"\nBASE=\"${TEX_FILE%.tex}\"\nRECORDER_FILE=\"${BASE}.fls\"\nAUX_FILE=\"${BASE}.aux\"\n\ncd \"$PAPER_DIR\"\n\nrun_sanitized() {\n  python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" run -- \"$@\"\n}\n\nrun_pdflatex() {\n  rm -f -- \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  set +e\n  run_sanitized pdflatex \\\n    -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error \"$TEX_FILE\"\n  local return_code=$?\n  set -e\n  if [ -f \"$RECORDER_FILE\" ]; then\n    python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" recorder \\\n      --paper-dir \"$PAPER_DIR\" --fls \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  elif [ \"$return_code\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    echo \"LaTeX recorder output missing: $PAPER_DIR/$RECORDER_FILE\" >&2\n    return 1\n  fi\n  return \"$return_code\"\n}\n\nrun_pdflatex\npython3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" bibtex \\\n  --paper-dir \"$PAPER_DIR\" --aux \"$AUX_FILE\"\nrun_sanitized bibtex \"$BASE\"\nrun_pdflatex\nrun_pdflatex\npython3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_rendered_si.py\" --pdf \"${BASE}.pdf\"\nVariance-Guided Benchmark Selection with Masked Low-Rank Score Models\nOn the two pinned leaderboard matrices, the retained variance-guided low-rank method has a higher pooled remaining-target prediction score than the tested baselines and loses score under historical-column derangement, supporting a conditional empirical result rather than universal benchmark sufficiency, response-adaptive selection, or fixed-target superiority.\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Variance-guided masked low-rank reconstruction\",\n    \"role\": \"proposed\",\n    \"include_reason\": \"The single studied method. Describe 'proposed' only as the contract role, not a novelty or search-improvement claim. The retained source learns masked factors and selects queries using a conditional trace-reduction proxy. Ground performance in final.evidence.episodes and final.metric.combined_score.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Random-query masked low-rank reconstruction\",\n    \"role\": \"ablation\",\n    \"include_reason\": \"The closest selector comparison: source inspection confirms the same factor-fitting and prediction construction with random available queries. A pooled paired family-clustered interval is available against this comparator; different remaining targets still prevent a fixed-target causal interpretation.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Information-selected covariance ridge\",\n    \"role\": \"baseline\",\n    \"include_reason\": \"Strongest pooled nonfactor comparator. It changes representation, regularization selection, and potentially query sets, so it is a joint pipeline comparison rather than a matched-query reconstruction ablation. Retain the Open LLM family-split seed where it slightly exceeds the studied method.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Correlation-medoid covariance ridge\",\n    \"role\": \"baseline\",\n    \"include_reason\": \"Tests a simpler correlation-centrality query ordering with covariance reconstruction; provides an interpretable selection comparator without adding an unevaluated method family.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Historical benchmark means\",\n    \"role\": \"baseline\",\n    \"include_reason\": \"Observation-invariant reference for the substantial predictability already present in historical task means. Its operational score is computed on its own query-policy remainder, not a universal zero-query target set.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Random-query mean-offset prediction\",\n    \"role\": \"baseline\",\n    \"include_reason\": \"Simple purchased-score reference: shift historical benchmark means by the observed mean residual. Distinguishes structured reconstruction from a global model-level offset.\"\n  }\n]\n{\n  \"mteb\": {\n    \"repository\": \"https://github.com/embeddings-benchmark/results\",\n    \"revision\": \"6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383\",\n    \"archive_sha256\": \"84773e577197630206eacc1790c5fd793d21393b698f6562b0a8f0a1ea31002f\",\n    \"license\": \"CC0-1.0 per task.md; pinned repository contains no standalone license file; no model inference or benchmark corpus included\"\n  },\n  \"open_llm\": {\n    \"repository\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/open-llm-leaderboard/contents\",\n    \"revision\": \"9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2\",\n    \"parquet_sha256\": \"f13a7061e63133bc8745d89f8c7a56148584940ede22d3b27e21cad1e078dca5\",\n    \"license\": \"Undeclared dataset license. Public unauthenticated access; private research extraction only, no asserted redistribution rights. Reacquire pinned public parquet for independent reproduction.\"\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"cases\": {\n    \"mteb/model/1009\": {\n      \"roster_hash\": \"5317f3b16b1788ea0f535ce1849e06983153a34a779b284ce4fb5a5af37ab6a2\",\n      \"historical_rows\": 177,\n      \"test_rows\": 52,\n      \"columns\": 172,\n      \"checkpoints\": [\n        1,\n        2,\n        4,\n        8\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mteb/model/1013\": {\n      \"roster_hash\": \"4703042bd53d996fe6ac2d94de9e578f895be8afd6eadb163a35ee8be0b2e861\",\n      \"historical_rows\": 177,\n      \"test_rows\": 51,\n      \"columns\": 172,\n      \"checkpoints\": [\n        1,\n        2,\n        4,\n        8\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mteb/model/1019\": {\n      \"roster_hash\": \"f6c64480540046b02f4c90b283c39296c7feba259bd06dd9c5623066e2a5c1f7\",\n      \"historical_rows\": 177,\n      \"test_rows\": 47,\n      \"columns\": 167,\n      \"checkpoints\": [\n        1,\n        2,\n        4,\n        8\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mteb/family/1009\": {\n      \"roster_hash\": \"001c0861aa46332a53208ee0cceaa79d558af8a735270652c5bc28ae98dfa4a3\",\n      \"historical_rows\": 164,\n      \"test_rows\": 58,\n      \"columns\": 156,\n      \"checkpoints\": [\n        1,\n        2,\n        4,\n        8\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mteb/family/1013\": {\n      \"roster_hash\": \"8fd274e8c525bfa81d2c0d4540f387ad2238d8ff1a7e3bde07180a6b2742c1f7\",\n      \"historical_rows\": 185,\n      \"test_rows\": 37,\n      \"columns\": 192,\n      \"checkpoints\": [\n        1,\n        2,\n        4,\n        8\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mteb/family/1019\": {\n      \"roster_hash\": \"5c8596a0f76723e9ad46936e5d4726d535cfd6886e6fadbb9db732d42b664c40\",\n      \"historical_rows\": 186,\n      \"test_rows\": 40,\n      \"columns\": 276,\n      \"checkpoints\": [\n        1,\n        2,\n        4,\n        8\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_llm/model/1009\": {\n      \"roster_hash\": \"edd5124dde36c7106ef64c804c470faada14afad388f9b559258e928ba568d2e\",\n      \"historical_rows\": 1833,\n      \"test_r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
