metric.paired_gain_ci_high\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": []},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Information-selected ridge scores 0.9482262260 (MAE 0.0517737740), with descriptive studied-minus-ridge difference 0.0045374631 and no supplied paired significance interval.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.selected_ridge_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.combined_score\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": []},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Medoid ridge scores 0.9327472830 (MAE 0.0672527170), mean offset 0.9206056682 (MAE 0.0793943318), and historical means 0.9068768878 (MAE 0.0931231122).\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.medoid_ridge_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.copy_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.constant_score\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": []},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"The studied method has the highest pooled observed score among the six evaluated policies, without statistical superiority being established against all comparators.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.combined_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.random_lowrank_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.selected_ridge_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.medoid_ridge_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.copy_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.constant_score\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": []},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Three final seeds are 1009, 1013, 1019; replay is excluded from primary means and figures.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"task/resources/final/plan.json#aggregation\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Figure 2, supplementary Table 2, and derived_results.json retain each of the twelve primary source/split/seed cells and six policies, using control=false and replay=false.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"build_paper_artifacts.py\\\", \\\"derived_results.json\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"The studied policy has higher observed scores than random-query factors in all twelve retained primary cells and the highest three-seed mean in each of four source/split conditions.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"derived_results.json#conditions\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Studied condition means are 0.9496/0.9442 for MTEB model/family splits and 0.9591/0.9582 for Open LLM model/family splits, rounded from saved observations.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"derived_results.json#conditions\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Pooled source scores are 0.9468974985 for MTEB and 0.9586298797 for Open LLM; they do not constitute controlled source-difficulty comparisons.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.mteb_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.open_llm_score\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": []},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Open LLM family split at seed 1019 gives studied score 0.9531041725 versus information-selected ridge 0.9533160600, a retained local reversal.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes[2].solution.cases\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Pooled independently deranged-history score is 0.9233917542 and actual-minus-control gap is 0.0293719349.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.permuted_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.corruption_gap\\\", \\\"final.metric.combined_score\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": []},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Every retained source/split/seed pair has a lower observed studied-policy score under historical-column derangement, as shown in Figure 3 and supplementary Table 3; the contrast changes learning, querying, and target composition jointly.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.corruption_gap\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"task/evaluate_final.py#permute_training\\\", \\\"tables/controls.tex\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"The final required cases completed and reset replay passed; these are interface/execution controls, not comprehensive validity guarantees.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.failed_episode_fraction\\\", \\\"final.metric.control_failure_fraction\\\", \\\"final.metric.reset_replay_ok\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": []},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Supplementary Figure 4 shows only the studied-policy measured checkpoint arrays, increasing in each retained actual trajectory; no baseline checkpoint comparison, fixed-panel curve, or universally sufficient budget is inferred.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": []},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Recorded seed durations are 24.0816306723, 22.8890082091, 23.0760153015 seconds, excluding independent acquisition; no measured inference-cost, end-to-end storage, or speed advantage is asserted.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": []},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"The inspectable retained source implements masked alternating ridge factors, fixed observed column means, and SVD initialization; lambda=0.1, candidate ranks 1/2/4/8, seeded 10% cell validation, at most four validation sweeps and eight refit sweeps capped by requested steps.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.selection_kind\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"Hoerl\\\", \\\"Koren\\\", \\\"Jain\\\"], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#L45-L83\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Equations 1 and 3 describe clipped remaining-target 1-MAE and context-independent ridge latent prediction; availability is known and historical missing cells are masked, not observed zeros.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.selection_kind\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"task/evaluate_final.py#curve_score\\\", \\\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#L110-L142\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"The retained-source acquisition in Equation 4 uses a unit-noise quadratic trace-reduction proxy, includes the queried coordinate, and ignores purchased score values. Equation 5 is a fixed-target matrix identity, not an MAE optimality theorem.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.selection_kind\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"Chaloner\\\", \\\"Cohn\\\"], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#L114-L127\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Random LF uses matching reference factor fit/prediction construction; the ridge comparators use zero-filled centered covariance and penalties 0.01/0.1/1 chosen with every-fifth-row historical validation; means and mean-offset policies use random legal queries.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.selection_kind\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"task/evaluate_final.py#reference_fit,predict_factors,run_baseline\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"The readable retained and original reference files match, but exact byte-level identity to the separately hashed final snapshot is not independently certified; mechanism interpretation is conditional on supplied-source association.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.selection_kind\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py\\\", \\\"source_evidence/downstream/baseline/src/program.py\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"The evaluated source regimes are separately fitted MTEB embedding-model scores and Open LLM six raw generative benchmark columns; no learned cross-source transfer is asserted.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"MTEB\\\"], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"task/resources/final/audit.json#sources,extraction\\\", \\\"task/evaluate_final.py#build_case\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Pinned MTEB revision is 6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383; pinned Open LLM revision is 9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2. MTEB extraction uses natural-bound original test scores and default/English task/revision/subset columns; Open LLM uses raw scores. The latter dataset license is undeclared.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"MTEB\\\"], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"task/resources/final/audit.json#sources,extraction\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"The inspected final protocol uses model and heuristic name-family disjoint groups, approximately 70% historical groups, twenty-observation MTEB column support, and coverage filters; family labels are not authoritative lineage.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"task/evaluate_final.py#split_components,require_disjoint_rows,build_case\\\", \\\"task/resources/final/audit.json#extraction\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"MTEB checkpoints are 1/2/4/8, Open LLM checkpoints 1/2/3. Target, row, checkpoint, seed, split, source weighting is nested and equal at each level; control/replay have zero primary weight.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"task/resources/final/plan.json#aggregation,production\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"The supplied interval uses 200 paired family-clustered bootstrap draws with RNG24681357 and 2.5/97.5 percentile endpoints, shared family multiplicities across paired policies, cases and seeds within source. It is preserved, not reconstructed from seed means.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_low\\\", \\\"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_high\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"Efron\\\", \\\"Owen\\\"], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"task/resources/final/plan.json#uncertainty\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Documented evaluation versions are CPython3.12.15, NumPy1.26.4, SciPy1.12.0, PyArrow16.1.0, with CPU operation, isolation and broker requirements; this is not a newly measured cross-platform reproduction.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"task/resources/final/plan.json#runtime\\\", \\\"task/requirements.txt\\\", \\\"task/evaluate_final.py#RPC\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"No fixed untouched target panel, response-adaptive selector, controlled nonlinear superiority, universal budget sufficiency, or family-held-out tuning is supported. Diagnostic descriptions remain unverified.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.attempts.unscored\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [], \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py\\\", \\\"task/resources/final/plan.json#limitations\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"MMLU, MTEB and HELM motivate heterogeneous evaluation coverage; item-level compression in tinyBenchmarks and metabench differs from buying aggregated benchmark scores; BenchBench motivates care about agreement methodology.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"ref.allowed.MMLU\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.MTEB\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.HELM\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.Tiny\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.Metabench\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.BenchBench\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"MMLU\\\", \\\"MTEB\\\", \\\"HELM\\\", \\\"Tiny\\\", \\\"Metabench\\\", \\\"BenchBench\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Observational scaling laws and Sloth motivate low-dimensional multi-benchmark capability descriptions, without establishing interpreted skill recovery or scaling-law estimation by this study.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"ref.allowed.Observational\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.Sloth\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"Observational\\\", \\\"Sloth\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Matrix factorization, probabilistic/Bayesian factor models, and implicit-feedback models provide distinct methodological precedents; this study fits regularized numerical-score coordinates rather than a fully Bayesian or implicit-preference model.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"ref.allowed.Koren\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.PMF\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.BayesianMF\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.Hu\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"Koren\\\", \\\"PMF\\\", \\\"BayesianMF\\\", \\\"Hu\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Convex, spectral, and alternating matrix completion methods have assumption-dependent guarantees that are not verified for the selectively observed matrices here.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"ref.allowed.CandesRecht\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.CandesTao\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.Keshavan\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.Mazumder\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.Jain\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"CandesRecht\\\", \\\"CandesTao\\\", \\\"Keshavan\\\", \\\"Mazumder\\\", \\\"Jain\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Ridge regularization, Bayesian design and statistical active learning are methodological context for the inspected solves and proxy, not evidence of novel architecture or universal MAE optimality.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"ref.allowed.Hoerl\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.Chaloner\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.Cohn\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"Hoerl\\\", \\\"Chaloner\\\", \\\"Cohn\\\"]},\n+    {\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Missing-data assumptions and incomplete-data likelihood methods are separate from merely optimizing a masked loss; generic bootstrap and dependent-array resampling motivate specifying the resampling unit.\\\", \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"ref.allowed.Rubin\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.Schafer\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.Dempster\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.Efron\\\", \\\"ref.allowed.Owen\\\"], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"Rubin\\\", \\\"Schafer\\\", \\\"Dempster\\\", \\\"Efron\\\", \\\"Owen\\\"]}\n+  ]\n+}\n*** Add File: README.md\n+# Variance-guided benchmark reconstruction: paper artifacts\n+\n+This directory contains \"'`paper.tex`, `paper.pdf`, `claims_grounding.json`, the inspectable retained implementation in `source_evidence/downstream/program/`, and saved evaluator evidence in `paper_data.json`. Performance measurements are frozen; manuscript preparation does not rerun them. Final qualification is **completed / qualified**, independently of the selection outcome. Three alternative evaluations have missing scores, not measured losses. The selected source is unchanged from the original reference. Exact final-snapshot byte identity is not certified: final and selection tree digests differ and a separate archived final source tree is unavailable.\n+\n+## Evidence and data\n+\n+- Model regimes: MTEB embedding models and Open LLM generative models, fitted independently.\n+- MTEB: https://github.com/embeddings-benchmark/results at `6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383`.\n+- Open LLM: https://huggingface.co/datasets/open-llm-leaderboard/contents at `9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2`.\n+- `task/resources/final/audit.json` specifies extraction, normalization, deduplication, source archive/table hashes, and license caveats. `task/resources/final/plan.json` specifies splits, frozen rosters, budgets, aggregation, uncertainty, and runtime.\n+- MTEB uses original bounded test main scores, default/English subsets, distinct task/revision/subset columns, and lexicographic revision tie-breaking. Open LLM uses six Raw columns. Follow the audit, not a current leaderboard or normalized score columns.\n+- Reacquire the MTEB archive via `https://github.com/embeddings-benchmark/results/archive/6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383.tar.gz`. For Open LLM, enumerate files via `https://huggingface.co/api/datasets/open-llm-leaderboard/contents/tree/9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2?recursive=true` and download the parquet using its revision-specific `/resolve/` URL. Compare SHA256 with the audit before extraction. No new acquisition is necessary to regenerate manuscript figures from the frozen summaries.\n+- Open LLM has an undeclared dataset license. Public access is not a redistribution license. The supplied extracted pool is a private research artifact; obtain source authorization before redistribution. Independently reacquire the pinned table.\n+- `task/` and `results/` are staged links to the accompanying run artifacts, not self-contained downloads. Preserve these directories alongside this manuscript when packaging the deliverables. All code used for this paper is present in the staged workspace, but this is not an assertion of public redistribution rights.\n+\n+## Regenerate static figures and tables\n+\n+Keep tools outside the manuscript tree, for example:\n+\n+```sh\n+python -m venv /tmp/paper-tools\n+/tmp/paper-tools/bin/pip install numpy==2.4.4 matplotlib==3.10.8 pillow==12.2.0 requests jsonschema pymupdf\n+/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python build_paper_artifacts.py\n+```\n+\n+The exact versions actually used are recorded in `paper_build_environment.txt` (prefer that snapshot over example commands if versions differ). No benchmark evaluation is run by this script. It reads numerical values from `paper_data.json`, excludes replay, exports vector PDF and 300-DPI PNG, and writes provenance sidecars. Approximate figure-generation time on this writing host is seconds; no portable runtime or peak-storage bound was measured.\n+\n+| Manuscript artifact | File / generator |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Figure 1, conceptual overview | `figures/concept_overview.png`; orchestrator-owned `generate-concept-figure` workflow; draft placeholder is guarded against overwriting a finished render |\n+| Figure 2, six-policy source/split comparison | `figures/main_comparison.pdf`; `build_paper_artifacts.py` |\n+| Figure 3, paired historical-column control | `figures/historical_dependence_control.pdf`; same script |\n+| Figure 4, supplementary checkpoint curves | `figures/budget_sensitivity.pdf`; same script |\n+| Table 1, pooled score and MAE | `tables/pooled.tex`; same script, included directly by LaTeX |\n+| Table 2, all primary seed scores | `tables/seed_scores.tex`; same script, its contents embedded in Supplementary Information for strict source validation |\n+| Table 3, all paired controls | `tables/controls.tex`; same script, contents embedded in Supplementary Information |\n+\n+`derived_results.json` holds unrounded descriptive means, standard deviations and individual saved scores. These are summaries of existing results, not new experiments. The supplied bootstrap interval is not recomputed from the three seed means.\n+\n+## Independent evaluation reproduction (not executed during writing)\n+\n+The recorded environment is CPython 3.12.15, NumPy 1.26.4, SciPy 1.12.0, PyArrow 16.1.0; see `task/requirements.txt`. A supported Linux x86-64 kernel with Landlock/seccomp and the trusted broker is required for the production isolation protocol. The native evaluation entrypoint accepts a **Python source file**, not a directory:\n+\n+```sh\n+python task/evaluate_final.py '\"\\\\\n+  --program_path source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py \\\\\n+  --results_dir /tmp/reproduced-final\n+\"'```\n+\n+This native invocation needs an appropriately isolated supported host; production used the broker-mediated interface. It is not a recipe for bypassing isolation. Fixed seeds are 1009, 1013, 1019; budgets are MTEB 1/2/4/8 and Open LLM 1/2/3. The final evaluator'\"'s wall limit is 3600 seconds; the saved seed durations are about 24.08, 22.89, and 23.08 seconds on the original host, not a prediction for other machines. Source acquisition is additional. Reruns should not overwrite \"'`paper_data.json` or the original final evidence. Missing baseline checkpoint arrays cannot be reconstructed from saved baseline averages.\n+\n+## Literature and manuscript build\n+\n+The 25 active references were restricted to exact allowed starter identifiers and foundational-method DOIs/titles. `references_provenance.json` records consulted abstracts and one full factorization paper. `literature/READING_NOTES.md` records rejected metadata and scope. No citation graph was expanded and no prohibited-material encounter was identified in this writing step. Re-retrieval is optional and does not affect frozen results:\n+\n+```sh\n+/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python retrieve_allowed_references.py\n+python .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py --tex paper.tex --bib references.bib\n+python .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py '\"\\\\\n+  --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json \\\\\n+  --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .\n+bash .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh verify --root-dir .\n+bash .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh paper.tex\n+\"'```\n+\n+The last command needs `pdflatex`, `bibtex`, and `pdftotext`. Use the supplied single-column ICLR review style without altering its geometry. Canonical system-root validation and figure validation may depend on orchestration modules absent in a minimal container; `validation_report.json` records actual checks and environment limitations rather than asserting unchecked success. Figure 1 remains a deliberately reserved placeholder until the orchestrator'\"'s synchronous render; the paper's quantitative figures and results are complete independently of it.\n+\n+The study compares changing-remainder policies, not fixed-target prediction, and does not establish response-adaptive acquisition, calibrated uncertainty, universal budget sufficiency, or speed superiority. Read the manuscript limitations before reusing inferred model scores.\n*** Add File: literature/READING_NOTES.md\n+# Restricted literature reading\n+\n+Only the 25 entries currently listed in \"'`references_provenance.json` are cited. Exact permitted starter IDs and exact foundational-method DOI/title lookups were used. Abstracts were read for relevance; the PMF source PDF was retrieved and its text inspected. No citation networks, related-paper lists, or broad benchmark-prediction searches were used. No prohibited-material encounter was identified during this paper-writing step.\n+\n+The original supplied bibliography was not used to fill the reference minimum: it largely concerned unrelated recommender applications. A lookup using arXiv 1001.3011 returned an unrelated variance-components title; that record was rejected and the intended spectral-regularization work was resolved by exact title. A title-search result for spectral regularization was also rejected because the returned title did not match. One service supplied a mechanical-device abstract for the EM paper; that content was rejected and the exact DOI was resolved through OpenAlex, whose abstract described incomplete-data likelihood correctly. These were metadata quality failures, not scientific evidence. Old uncited lookup files are not active bibliography entries.\n+\n+Claims were limited to the consulted content: evaluation breadth, item-versus-benchmark measurement granularity, low-dimensional modeling, matrix-completion assumptions, ridge regularization, prediction-oriented design, missingness, and resampling dependence. No literature results were used as measurements in this study, and no novelty claim against inaccessible or prohibited prior work was made.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/pip freeze > paper_build_environment.txt\npython .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
